# .gitignore for Android projects
# ════════════════════════════════
# Files and folders listed here are NOT tracked by git.
# They are either generated by the build system (can be recreated),
# local to one developer's machine, or contain private/sensitive data.

# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The 'build' folder is entirely generated — it's the compiled output.
# Checking it in would bloat the repo and cause constant merge conflicts.
/build
app/build

# ── Local configuration ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# local.properties is generated by Android Studio and contains paths specific
# to YOUR machine (e.g. where the Android SDK is installed).
# Every developer has a different one, so it must never be shared.
local.properties

# ── Android Studio IDE files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .idea/ contains Android Studio's project settings (window positions, run configs, etc.).
# Most of these are personal and machine-specific.
# Note: some teams DO commit .idea/ — this is a project choice. Ignoring it keeps
# the repo clean for a solo/small-team project.
.idea/
*.iws
*.iml
*.ipr

# ── Gradle cache ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .gradle/ is Gradle's local cache of downloaded dependencies and build artefacts.
# It is regenerated automatically when you build.
.gradle

# ── Keystore / signing files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEVER commit signing keys to version control — anyone with the key can publish
# to the Play Store as you. These are listed as a reminder, not because they
# exist yet (Milestone 1 uses the debug keystore managed by Android Studio).
*.jks
*.keystore

# ── Generated files ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
gen/
out/

# ── macOS metadata ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
